// arm_divergence — "four arms ask the checker and the fifth does not".
//
// ── WHY THIS RULE AND NOT ANOTHER ───────────────────────────────────────────
// Seven of eight borrow-check fixes in one week were A CALL THAT WAS NOT MADE,
// not machinery that was missing:
//   field_borrow_conflicts existed and was reached from four mutating sites of
//   five; outliving_params_ drew the right line and was read at one site of
//   eleven; dying_binding was written and not read twenty lines above.
// None is findable by grep, because each is an ABSENCE. An absence over a finite
// domain is derivable — that is the whole premise of tools/dlog.
//
// ⚠ AND UNLIKE THE PLACE-WALKER RULE, THIS ONE NEEDS NO CLAIM. `spelling_keyed`
// has to be told what a projection is and what a walker is; those are human
// assertions living in not_projection.claim and in a derivation. Here the domain
// is SELF-SUPPLYING: the arms of one switch are each other's control. If nine
// arms of a dispatcher call the conflict check and the tenth does not, the nine
// are the specification and nothing had to be declared.
.decl tests(f: symbol, k: symbol, pos: symbol)
.decl arm_call(f: symbol, k: symbol, callee: symbol)
.decl callee_home(callee: symbol, file: symbol)
.input tests
.input arm_call
.input callee_home

// ── WHAT COUNTS AS A CHECK: A PROPERTY, NOT A NAME LIST ─────────────────────
// The first run drowned. Its seven sharpest rows were `push_back`, `operand`,
// `receiver` and `operator=` — structural readers, whose absence from an arm
// says only that the arm has a different SHAPE, which is the premise, not a
// finding. Excluding them by name would be the enumeration disease committed
// inside the detector, for the third time in this directory.
// So exclude by WHERE THE CALLEE IS DEFINED: a view accessor lives in
// lir_view.hpp, a container method in the standard library. What remains is
// compiler logic, and the set moves on its own when a file is added.
.decl structural(callee: symbol)
structural(P) :- callee_home(P, "lir_view.hpp").
structural(P) :- callee_home(P, "lir_schema.hpp").
structural(P) :- callee_home(P, F), !compiler_file(F).
.decl compiler_file(file: symbol)
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains(".cpp", F).
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains(".inc", F).
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains("sema", F).
compiler_file(F) :- callee_home(_, F), contains("borrow", F).

// Only LIVE arms are peers. An empty label runs nothing, so "it does not call
// the checker" is trivially true of it and says nothing about the author.
.decl arm(f: symbol, k: symbol)
arm(F, K) :- tests(F, K, "case_live").

.decl arm_count(f: symbol, n: number)
arm_count(F, N) :- arm(F, _), N = count : { arm(F, _K) }.

// How many of F's live arms call P at all.
.decl callers(f: symbol, callee: symbol, n: number)
callers(F, P, N) :- arm_call(F, _, P),
                    N = count : { arm_call(F, K, P), arm(F, K) }.

// The finding: arm K of F does not call P, while at least two of its peers do.
// Two, not one — a single peer is an anecdote, and this rule has no oracle other
// than agreement among siblings.
//
// ⚠ THIS RANKS, IT DOES NOT JUDGE. An arm legitimately skips a check all the
// time: the code is unreachable there, the type cannot carry a borrow, the
// callee is meaningless for that shape. The output is a reading list ordered by
// how lonely the silent arm is, and every row still needs a one-variable
// control before it is a defect. Three of the first candidates from the sister
// rule were false positives, one documented in its own comment.
.decl divergent(f: symbol, k: symbol, callee: symbol, called: number, total: number)
.output divergent
divergent(F, K, P, C, T) :- arm(F, K), callers(F, P, C), C >= 2,
                            !arm_call(F, K, P), arm_count(F, T), C < T,
                            !structural(P), P != F.

// A dispatcher where exactly ONE arm is the odd one out for some callee is the
// sharpest shape of all, and it is what try_path and #139 both were.
.decl lone_silent_arm(f: symbol, k: symbol, callee: symbol, total: number)
.output lone_silent_arm
lone_silent_arm(F, K, P, T) :- divergent(F, K, P, C, T), C = T - 1.
